== Notes == 
This answer is in the form of a poem, with each line representing a different sentence.
The story is about two Native American men from the Egulac tribe who go to the city to sell their horses and are mistaken for thieves.
One night two men from Egulac came to the city;
They went to the place where the horses were bought and sold;
The people there knew them not, and they knew not them;
They wondered why these strange men came to the city;
They wondered if these strange men were up to no good;
The people talked and made up stories about these men;
One night two men from Egulac left the city;
They went back to their people, to their tents and their wigwams;
The people of Egulac asked them what had happened;
They told how they had been taken for thieves in the city;
How they had been accused and nearly beaten by the city folks;
How they had been saved by a white man, a friend of theirs;
One night two men from Egulac lived to tell the tale. 

